# DeepGrooveBallBearing.FCMacro
#
# Usage:
#   1. Select a circular edge, or nothing at all.
#   2. Run the macro. A task panel opens next to the 3D view (the view stays usable) with
#      a live preview of the bearing, and you choose how to get the races:
#      - "Groove selected body": the ball groove is cut into the PartDesign Body the edge
#        belongs to, and the body itself becomes the races. On a bore, the bore is the
#        bearing's ID: a thin inner race is split off and the rest of the body is the
#        outer race (with the ball groove). On an outer surface it is the other way
#        round. A plain ring simply becomes the inner and outer race.
#      - "Create races": a new ring with both races is built. The edge (on anything,
#        e.g. a shaft or a housing bore) sets the bearing's position, axis and either
#        its ID or its OD. With nothing selected, it is created at the origin on Z.
#        Races, cage and balls go into one App::Part labelled with the bearing's size,
#        e.g. "Bearing 32x20x8" (OD x ID x Height), or "Bearing 608 (22x8x7)" for a
#        catalog size; move the Part to move the bearing.
#   3. Pick a catalog size (608, 625, ...) or enter ID / OD / height, pick a ball preset
#      or enter the ball diameter, and set the number of balls and the cage/ball
#      options. A status line says what doesn't fit. On OK a sketch is created in a
#      plane containing the bearing axis, and one PartDesign Groove cuts it around that
#      axis, splitting the blank into the (disconnected) inner and outer races.
#   4. Optionally a snap-in cage is built in a separate "Cage" Body between the races,
#      and the balls in a separate "Balls" Body (off by default).
#
# Parameters live on a "BearingParameters" datum coordinate system inside the races
# Body (one per bearing). Select it in the tree to edit:
#   Bearing: ID, OD, Height, BallDiameter, NumBalls  (the edge's diameter is read-only
#            when grooving the selected body)
#   Cage:    CageThickness, CageTopOffset, PocketClearance, PocketRise
#
# The datum is the bearing frame: origin on the axis at mid-height, Z = bearing axis.
# The groove sketch is attached to its XZ plane, and the Cage and Balls bodies follow it.
#
# Groove profile (deep-groove-bb.FCStd / Sketch001):
#   - Ball circle (construction), centered at the pitch diameter, mid-height
#   - Slot of width = ball diameter / 2, centered on the ball, through the full height
#   - Outline = the slot walls + the ball arcs that bulge into each race
#
# Cage (deep-groove-bb.FCStd / Cage body):
#   - Ring of CageThickness centered on the pitch diameter, from the bottom face up to
#     CageTopOffset below where the slot walls meet the ball
#   - Ball pocket of Ø (BallDiameter + PocketClearance), rising PocketRise above the
#     cage top (snap-in opening), polar-patterned NumBalls times
#   - Shown seated: in use the balls pull the cage along the axis until the pockets are
#     centered on them, so the whole cage is shifted by that amount (it then sits
#     slightly inside the races). This holds whether or not the balls are modelled.
#
# Balls:
#   - Sphere of BallDiameter at the pitch diameter, mid-height (in line with the cage
#     pockets), polar-patterned NumBalls times
#
# Sketch coordinate system (groove and cage sketches):
#   - Origin  : on the bearing axis, at mid-height
#   - X axis  : radial direction (outward)
#   - Y axis  : bearing axis (V_Axis) -- grooves and revolutions turn around this
#
# The same 3D-printable bearing is part of the Bearings workbench for FreeCAD, which
# adds standard (bought) bearings and a bearing search. This macro is kept in step with
# the workbench's printable bearing.

import math
import textwrap

import FreeCAD as App
import Part
import Sketcher

V = App.Vector
TITLE = "Deep Groove Ball Bearing"
CUSTOM = "Custom"

TOL = 1e-6
PARAMS = "BearingParameters"
GROOVE = "Groove selected body"
CREATE = "Create races"
SIN60 = math.sqrt(3) / 2  # slot = ball Ø / 2, so the slot walls meet the ball at 60°
# What each parameter means: the datum's property descriptions and the dialog tooltips
BEARING_DOCS = {
    "ID": "Bore of the inner race, i.e. the shaft diameter the bearing fits on.",
    "OD": "Outside diameter of the outer race, i.e. the housing bore the bearing fits in.",
    "Height": "Axial width of the bearing (B in bearing catalogues). The balls and race "
    "grooves are centered in it.",
    "BallDiameter": "Diameter of the balls. The balls run on the pitch diameter, midway between "
    "ID and OD, and the gap between the two races is half the ball diameter. "
    "Must be smaller than the ring wall, (OD - ID) / 2, and than the height.",
    "NumBalls": "How many balls (and cage pockets) are spaced evenly around the bearing. "
    "The maximum depends on the ball size and the pitch diameter.",
}
DEFAULT_NUM_BALLS = 10
DEFAULT_BALL_DIAMETER = 4.0
